regress/artifacts\lcashiftub\pass2_c7d7414\ollama_glm.txt:45:NOT SETTLEABLE FROM PACKET — the packet inlines one hunk. But REASONED from the packet's own names: the red control row is called **`lcaconfbus1kill`**, which implies the conf handler has a **bus==1 arm** — the `else` below the fixed line — plausibly with its own device-bit scan. If it uses the same `0x800 << dev` shape, the identical UB sits in the same function, unfixed and (per P4) undetected. Census boundary for the class (REASONED): an unsuffixed constant overflows when (top bit index of constant) + (max shift) > 30; 0x800 is bit 11 with dev to 20 — exactly one past the boundary. The census should start with this function/file and must exclude the three pristine copies or drown in 2021 duplicates. **Settling fact: `grep -n '<<' src/devices/dev_lca.c` in this tree.**
