< lsb' population.  At width 0 the shift `1 << 0' is DEFINED and the mask becomes 0 -- semantically wrong, not undefined.  glm derived it from the brief's own width formula; grok reached it separately; codex confirmed.  The conclusion is unchanged and the number had already propagated into four records, all corrected. ***  AND MY OWN PATCH INVALIDATED MY OWN CITATIONS: grok noted the brief's decoder cites were the PRE-comment line numbers; after the diff they moved, and after the pass-2 edits they moved again -- THREE VALUES IN ONE EVENING for one unchanged expression, which is why no line number for it appears in the CHANGELOG block.  FOLLOW-UP SHIPPED SEPARATELY (probe half applied, source half is comment-only): `s w32 pc' and `s w31' added, because SBFX at width 31 was UNTESTED and the round's headline claim -- "only the width-32 case is observable" -- rested on a UBFX width-31 row and generalised to SBFX with no evidence.  bfi at cpu_arm_instr.c X(bfi) DELIBERATELY UNTOUCHED and disclosed: it carries the same shift-UB shape and is out of this round's scope by the one-site rule.
