regress/artifacts\lunaabsentcpu\pass3_panel_20260906_102412\kimi.txt:159:  Candidate: #9, es438 discharged. "es438: its owed mask2/mask3 pair is discharged by this detector's rows — annotate/close on this round." Hmm — es438 is a ledger row; the probe has mask2/mask3 readback rows (declined-store checks). Pass-2 grok said "es438cells" is not a ledger row — "es438 is the row". The disposition says the owed mask2/mask3 pair is discharged by THIS detector's rows. Is that wrong? The mask readback rows test that stores to ABSENT slots are kept as storage with readback — that's lunaabsentmaskdecl territory. es438 might be about something else (the ES438... hmm, "es438" might be a row about the mask registers' cell behavior on PRESENT slots, or about interrupt_enable readback on a -n 4 machine?). Without the ledger I can't be sure. This is suspicious — cross-row discharge is a classic ledger-laundering move. The mask2/mask3 readback rows in THIS probe are on absent slots (1-cpu machine). If es438's owed pair was about present slots (e.g., on a multi-cpu machine, MASK2 readback), then this detector's rows don't discharge it. Hmm.
