carefully:\n\n```diff\n-#if 0\n+\t\tcase M88K_EXCEPTION_MISALIGNED_ACCESS:\n+\t\tcase M88K_EXCEPTION_UNIMPLEMENTED_OPCODE:\n+\t\tcase M88K_EXCEPTION_PRIVILEGE_VIOLATION:\n+\t\tcase M88K_EXCEPTION_BOUNDS_CHECK_VIOLATION:\n \t\tcase M88K_EXCEPTION_ILLEGAL_INTEGER_DIVIDE:\n-\t\t\t/*  TODO: Is it correct to continue on the instruction\n-\t\t\t    _after_ the division by zero? Or should the PC\n-\t\t\t    be backed up one step?  */\n+\t\tcase M88K_EXCEPTION_INTEGER_OVERFLOW:\n+\t\tcase M88K_EXCEPTION_ERROR:\n+\t\t\t/*  m88kexcdeliver: the common path above is already the\n+\t\t\t    ... */\n \t\t\tbreak;\n-#endif\n```\n\nHmm, interesting. So originally the structure was:\n\n```c\n#if 0\n\t\tcase M88K_EXCEPTION_ILLEGAL_INTEGER_DIVIDE:\n\t\t\t/*  TODO: Is it correct to continue on the instruction\n\t\t\t    _after_ the division by zero? Or should the PC\n\t\t\t    be backed up one step?  */\n\t\t\tbreak;\n#endif\n```\n\nAnd now:\n\n```c\n\t\tcase M88K_EXCEPTION_MISALIGNED_ACCESS:\n\t\tcase M88K_EXCEPTION_UNIMPLEMENTED_OPCODE:\n\t\tcase M88K_EXCEPTION_PRIVILEGE_VIOLATION:\n\t\tcase M88K_EXCEPTION_BOUNDS_CHECK_VIOLATION:\n\t\tcase M88K_EXCEPTION_ILLEGAL_INTEGER_DIVIDE:\n\t\tcase M88K_EXCEPTION_INTEGER_OVERFLOW:\n\t\tcase M88K_EXCEPTION_ERROR:\n\t\t\t/*  comment  */\n\t\t\tbreak;\n```\n\nSo the seven tail labels match the seven switch-1 arms. Good.\n\nWait, the hunk header says `@@ -896,13 +915,29 @@` \u2014 13 lines removed context-ish, 29 added. The `#if 0` and `#endif` lines removed. OK.\n\nNow, the question of the tail switch: does the tail switch handle other vectors with arms that do something else (e.g., RESET arm)? From the packet: \"Vector 0 named by a trap dies in the tail RESET arm (filed separately).\" So the tail switch has a RESET arm for vector 0 which stops (or something bad). That's filed separately as `m88kexcresetkill`.\n\nAlso there's an `#if 0` SFU1 block below the new arms, unchanged.\n\n## The contract\n\nThe contract per MC88100 UM:\n- rte resumes at S