regress/artifacts\m88kexcdeliver\pass2_panel_20260905_212630\kimi.txt:446:  Also **the big one I noticed**: The tail comment says "ERROR arrives here from the SFRZ re-route above with the shadows deliberately frozen (update_shadow_regs false)". TRUE for the re-route path. But ERROR ALSO arrives via errortb (trap naming 10) with update_shadow_regs TRUE. The sentence says "ERROR arrives here from the SFRZ re-route" — as the sole described route, incomplete but the errortb route is the "normal" one (trap naming vector 10 directly). Is the sentence FALSE? It says "ERROR arrives here from the SFRZ re-route above with the shadows deliberately frozen" — for the errortb path, shadows are NOT frozen (EPSR updated). The sentence is about the re-route arrival, which is accurate; it doesn't claim it's the only route. Borderline: "ERROR arrives here from the SFRZ re-route above" could be read as "when ERROR arrives, it's from the re-route" — which the errortb row disproves (measured: errortb delivers with normal shadow update). Q1 asks "Is anything in the tail arm's comment FALSE?" — this is a candidate: the sentence is incomplete (not the only route) but not false as written. Also "the one-site fix was measured to do exactly that" — check opus_logs for that measurement (one-site form halting at tail default). There's x_D1_*.out and table_D1.out — plausible.
regress/artifacts\m88kexcdeliver\pass2_panel_20260905_212630\kimi.txt:452:  Wait, actually pre-fix, were the seven stopped by the FALLBACK (all CPUs)? Yes: pre-fix, implemented stayed false for the seven → fallback fired → stop all. The tail default was only reached if implemented=true in switch 1 but no tail label — pre-fix that combination didn't exist for the seven. The MEASURED "one-site fix" (implemented=true without tail labels) reaches tail default → stops this cpu with registers set. OK.
