regress/artifacts\m88kexcdeliver\opus_p2.md:42:**Q1 — Is the diff right?** Yes. I read `m88k_exception()` end to end and checked every hunk. The seven arms are the right seven: they are exactly the trap-like classes with a defined delivery contract, and adding both sites (switch-1 `implemented` **and** a tail label) is required — M_IMPLOVF (9/10) and M_ERRORTAIL (8/10) each pin one site independently, and M_NAIVE (0/9) pins the pair. The INFO level is right and follows the file's own idiom: the four already-delivered classes print at `VERBOSITY_INFO`, `default_verbosity = VERBOSITY_INFO` (`src/core/debugmsg.c:104`), and INTERRUPT already prints unbounded on every boot — so the seven are joining an accepted precedent, not creating a new hazard. I verified the hygiene premise myself: `grep -i exception regress/gate_hygiene.sh` gives one hit, an unrelated comment at `:92`, and **no gate script anywhere greps for any of the seven class names**.
